    values:originalText "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:  (a) personal information that relates to an individual is disclosed to the first person because of the operation of this Part; and  (b) the first person subsequently discloses the personal information; and  Privacy Act 1988  Schedule 1  (c) the first person is not responsible for the individual (within the meaning of subclause 2.5 of Schedule 3). Penalty: 60 penalty units or imprisonment for 1 year, or both." ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer .

concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80q-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "80Q(2) Disclosure of information—offence"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-80q-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the following disclosures:  (a) if the first person is an agency—a disclosure permitted under an Information Privacy Principle;  (b) if the first person is an organisation—a disclosure permitted under an approved privacy code or a National Privacy Principle;  (c) a disclosure permitted under section 80P;  (d) a disclosure made with the consent of the individual to whom the personal information relates;  (e) a disclosure to the individual to whom the personal information relates;  (f) a disclosure to a court;  (g) a disclosure prescribed by the regulations. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in subsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the following disclosures:  (a) if the first person is an agency—a disclosure permitted under an Information Privacy Principle;  (b) if the first person is an organisation—a disclosure permitted under an approved privacy code or a National Privacy Principle;  (c) a disclosure permitted under section 80P;  (d) a disclosure made with the consent of the individual to whom the personal information relates;  (e) a disclosure to the individual to whom the personal information relates;  (f) a disclosure to a court;  (g) a disclosure prescribed by the regulations. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in subsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "824e1f2caa80aa1d4d2c4bedafba06361a3d890e7edab307937951a425638541" ;
    values:partOf concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80q ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Disclosure of information is permitted under certain conditions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
